{"sounds":{"intro":"This is Old English (Anglo-Saxon) as written around the year 1000, the language of Beowulf and King Alfred. It looks foreign but its words are the roots of English. The spelling here is the normalised one used in textbooks, with bars over long vowels. Nobody speaks it, so the pronunciation is a scholars' reconstruction.","rows":[["þ / ð","like \"th\" in \"thing\" or \"this\"","þæt, ðæt"],["æ","like \"a\" in \"cat\"","æppel"],["ā / ē / ī / ō / ū","the same vowels, held long","hūs"],["ċ","like \"ch\" in \"church\"","ċild"],["ġ","like \"y\" in \"yes\"","ġē"],["sc","like \"sh\" in \"ship\"","scip"],["h","a rough breath at the start; like \"ch\" in \"loch\" after a vowel","niht"],["f / s / þ","voiced (v, z, th in \"this\") between vowels, voiceless elsewhere","hlāford"]],"notes":["All the letters are said, including the \"k\" in \"cniht\" (knight) and the \"h\" in \"hlāf\" (loaf).","Old English has four cases, three genders and a different \"you\" for one (þū) and many (ġē).","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. Only well-attested words and forms are included. Nothing has been checked by a specialist, so treat it as a first guide."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","ān","ahn","ān"],["two","twā","twah","twā"],["three","þrīe","THREE-eh","þrīe"],["four","fēower","FAY-oh-wer","fēower"],["five","fīf","feef","fīf"],["six","siex","SEE-eks","siex"],["seven","seofon","SAY-oh-von","seofon"],["eight","eahta","EH-ahk-tah","eahta"],["nine","nigon","NI-gon","nigon"],["ten","tīen","TEE-en","tīen"]]},{"id":"bigger-numbers","title":"Bigger numbers","items":[["twenty","twēntig","TWAY-n-tig","twēntig"],["one hundred","hund","hoond","hund"],["one thousand","þūsend","THOO-send","þūsend"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"hello-and-goodbye","title":"Hello and goodbye","items":[["hello","hāl","hahl","hāl"],["be well","wes þū hāl","wes thoo hahl","wes þū hāl"],["good morning","gōd morgen","gohd MOR-gen","gōd morgen"],["farewell","fare þū wel","FAH-reh thoo wel","fare þū wel"]]},{"id":"meeting","title":"Meeting","items":[["how are you?","hū fært þū","hoo fehrt thoo","hū fært þū?"],["I am well","ic eom gōd","ik ay-om gohd","ic eom gōd"],["what is your name?","hwæt is þīn nama","hwat is theen NAH-mah","hwæt is þīn nama?"],["my name is...","mīn nama is","meen NAH-mah is","mīn nama is"],["where are you from?","hwanon eart þū","HWAH-non ehrt thoo","hwanon eart þū?"],["I am from England","ic eom of Englalande","ik ay-om of ENG-lah-lahn-deh","ic eom of Englalande"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"essential-phrases","title":"Essential phrases","items":[["yes","ġēa","yay-ah","ġēa"],["no","nā","nah","nā"],["thank you","ic þancie þē","ik THAHN-ki-eh theh","ic þancie þē"],["I know","ic wāt","ik waht","ic wāt"],["I do not know","ic ne wāt","ik neh waht","ic ne wāt"],["I understand","ic understande","ik oon-der-STAHN-deh","ic understande"],["I do not understand","ic ne understande","ik neh oon-der-STAHN-deh","ic ne understande"],["what is this?","hwæt is þis","hwat is this","hwæt is þis?"],["where is...?","hwǣr is","hwair is","hwǣr is"],["I want","ic wille","ik WIL-leh","ic wille"],["I do not want","ic nylle","ik NUL-leh","ic nylle"],["I love","ic lufie","ik LOO-vi-eh","ic lufie"]]},{"id":"about-me","title":"About me","items":[["I am a man","ic eom mann","ik ay-om mahn","ic eom mann"],["I have a book","ic hæbbe bōc","ik HAB-beh bohk","ic hæbbe bōc"],["I see","ic sēo","ik say-oh","ic sēo"],["I hear","ic hīere","ik HEE-eh-reh","ic hīere"],["I say","ic cweþe","ik KWEH-theh","ic cweþe"],["I write","ic wrīte","ik WREE-teh","ic wrīte"],["I eat","ic ete","ik EH-teh","ic ete"],["I drink","ic drince","ik DRIN-cheh","ic drince"]]},{"id":"asking","title":"Asking","items":[["who?","hwā","hwah","hwā?"],["what?","hwæt","hwat","hwæt?"],["where?","hwǣr","hwair","hwǣr?"],["when?","hwenne","HWEN-neh","hwenne?"],["why?","for hwȳ","for hwee","for hwȳ?"],["how?","hū","hoo","hū?"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and fami